# SEO & Metadata Skill

## Purpose
TBE-Web uses a custom `<SEO>` component (Next.js `<Head>`) with JSON-LD structured data support. Every public-facing page must have SEO meta. This skill ensures canonical URLs, Open Graph tags, and JSON-LD schemas are set correctly and consistently.

## Rules
1. **Every public page must render `<SEO seoMeta={seoMeta} />`** from `@tbe/components` inside `<Fragment>`.
2. **`seoMeta` must come from `getPreFetchProps`** via `getStaticProps` or `getServerSideProps` — never hardcode meta strings in components.
3. **For Course pages, add `schema={{ type: "Course", course: { ... } }}`** to the `<SEO>` component.
4. **For FAQ sections, add `schema={{ type: "FAQPage", faq: [...] }}`**.
5. **For article/blog/webinar pages, add `schema={{ type: "Article", article: { ... } }}`**.
6. **Always include `appId` from `@tbe/constants` `AppIdentifier`** in the SEO component — this determines the favicon.
7. **Canonical URLs are generated automatically** by the SEO component from `useRouter().asPath` — never set `<link rel="canonical">` manually.
8. **Open Graph images must be absolute URLs** — use `STATIC_FILE_PATH` from `@tbe/constants` for path construction.
9. **`next-sitemap` config is in each app's `next-sitemap.config.js`** — never manually manage sitemap.xml files.
10. **Dynamic pages must be excluded from static sitemap if data-dependent** — add to `exclude` in `next-sitemap.config.js`.

## Patterns

### Basic page with SEO
```tsx
import { SEO } from "@tbe/components";
import type { PageProps } from "@tbe/interface";
import { getPreFetchProps } from "@tbe/utils";
import type { GetStaticProps } from "next";
import { Fragment } from "react";

const AboutPage = ({ seoMeta }: PageProps) => {
  return (
    <Fragment>
      <SEO seoMeta={seoMeta} appId="platform" />
      {/* page content */}
    </Fragment>
  );
};

export const getStaticProps: GetStaticProps = async () => {
  return await getPreFetchProps({ pageId: "about" });
};

export default AboutPage;
```

### Course page with JSON-LD
```tsx
const CoursePage = ({ seoMeta, course }: CoursePageProps) => {
  return (
    <Fragment>
      <SEO
        seoMeta={seoMeta}
        appId="platform"
        schema={{
          type: "Course",
          course: {
            name: course.title,
            description: course.description,
            provider: "The Boring Education",
            url: `https://www.theboringeducation.com/courses/${course.slug}`,
            skillLevel: course.difficulty,
          },
        }}
      />
      {/* course content */}
    </Fragment>
  );
};
```

### FAQ page with JSON-LD
```tsx
<SEO
  seoMeta={seoMeta}
  schema={{
    type: "FAQPage",
    faq: [
      { question: "What is TBE?", answer: "The Boring Education is..." },
      { question: "How do I enroll?", answer: "Click Get Started..." },
    ],
  }}
/>
```

### Breadcrumb schema
```tsx
<SEO
  seoMeta={seoMeta}
  schema={{
    type: "BreadcrumbList",
    breadcrumbs: [
      { name: "Home", url: "https://www.theboringeducation.com/" },
      { name: "Courses", url: "https://www.theboringeducation.com/shiksha" },
      { name: course.title, url: `https://www.theboringeducation.com/shiksha/${course.slug}` },
    ],
  }}
/>
```

## Anti-Patterns

### ❌ Hardcoded meta tags in component
```tsx
// BAD
const CoursePage = () => (
  <>
    <Head>
      <title>React Course | TBE</title>
      <meta name="description" content="Learn React..." />
    </Head>
    {/* ... */}
  </>
);
```
```tsx
// GOOD — meta comes from API via getPreFetchProps
const CoursePage = ({ seoMeta }: PageProps) => (
  <Fragment>
    <SEO seoMeta={seoMeta} appId="platform" />
    {/* ... */}
  </Fragment>
);
```

### ❌ Manual canonical tag
```tsx
// BAD
<Head>
  <link rel="canonical" href="https://www.theboringeducation.com/courses/react" />
</Head>
```
```tsx
// GOOD — SEO component handles canonical automatically from router
<SEO seoMeta={seoMeta} appId="platform" />
```
